# Monday's run of record, the served node's settings (served_verdicts.sh reads it after remote_run.sh's exports):
# remote's own private file, then its one load sent through the network certifier on vy-auditor-2. OF_RECORD makes the
# preflight refuse the run lacking any input its onsite record's of_record reads, here and again in the follow-on.
. /workspace/research/vllm-served-verdicts/settings-remote/settings.env
LOAD=front OF_RECORD=1
# Untied remote-network-no-pouw at V3c's subset:1 (C-Flock --zk): untied, PoUW's period case can't name R, so the
# composite is the one without PoUW. COMPOSITE stays unset: the follow-on composes it, and the composite is the record's
# verdict. ALPHA and GAMMA unset: the inference-only case reads them off the division (--from-division).
# V3c's class is one link-window of the gate's w63k4 schedule (T 32, EVERY 16, 4 lanes): 2 boundaries of 4 lanes, all
# five fields (8,32,4 alone defaults its lanes to 8, one boundary). CLASSES holds it, so step 3 writes V3c's record at it.
PRODUCT=remote-network-no-pouw H1_TIE= V3C_CLASS=8,32,4,4,16 CLASSES=8,32,4,4,16 V3C_LAW=subset:1
POUW_CMD=
# H1's period, its window-0 reserve and the gate check go under onsite's own gate lane, network-accounting, whose key on
# this node the gate takes the lane from; never lane vllm's key. remote_run.sh's start reads take the same key.
H1_GATE="ssh -i $HOME/.ssh/vy-gate-network-accounting -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=30 research@204.12.178.84" H1_LANE=network-accounting
# Untied, this node commits the window after the serve, and the follow-on audits that commit: 120m for an 8-slot commit,
# WC_TIMEOUT 60m for the class's window-circuit record and inference-only policy, which lower the class once a slot
V3C_TIMEOUT=120m WC_TIMEOUT=60m
# The serve is refused where the serve dir's filesystem has fewer free inodes than this (served_verdicts.sh's floor,
# stated here so the run's settings carry it): the class window the commit writes takes several hundred thousand
MIN_FREE_INODES=500000
# The follow-on's caps, 24 h together inside its job's --timeout of 108000 s (30 h), which leaves about 6 h for the copy
# and the record: V3c's audit 13h (every template composed one after another, then subset:1's one member, its session
# and its Lean check), the chain 4h, the period step 1h (network-period in full: this tree's certifier_piece.py takes no
# --case-only) and the composite 6h. Here they bind nothing, since this node defers all four; the follow-on doesn't read
# this file, and follow_launch.sh's CAPS passes these (--env), over reproof_follow.sh's defaults
V3C_AUDIT_TIMEOUT=13h CERTIFIER_TIMEOUT=4h CERTIFIER_PERIOD_TIMEOUT=1h COMPOSITE_TIMEOUT=6h
# The network certifier's piece split around V3c, both steps in the follow-on: the chain with the scan on V3c's
# committed window, then the period check on V3c's period.json, network-period in full, after V3c's audit has freed its
# memory; no --circuit, which is H1_TIE's
CERTIFIER_CHAIN_CMD='"$PY" benchmarks/network_traces/certifier_piece.py chain "$@" --certifier-key "${CERTIFIER_KEY:-}"'
CERTIFIER_PERIOD_CMD='"$PY" benchmarks/network_traces/certifier_piece.py period "$@" --certifier-key "${CERTIFIER_KEY:-}"'
# Prompts of 8 to 32 ids; no --stop-prompt, since at one token a warm-up ends on EOS only if its first token is EOS
CERTIFIER_FRONT='"$PY" benchmarks/network_traces/certifier_piece.py front "$1" "$2" "$3" --gate research@vy-auditor-2 --peer vy-dc-h200-2 --prompts "$SLOTS" --prompt-ids 8:32 --tokens "$MAX_TOKENS" --bucket-ms 4000'
# The follow-on alone takes PP_CHALLENGER, PP_PEER and PP_CHALLENGER_KEY, CERTIFIER_GATE, CERTIFIER_PEER and
# CERTIFIER_PIN, and writes CERTIFIER_KEY and SITE_REGISTRATION (follow_launch.sh's --env, reproof_follow.sh): nothing
# here sets them
